{"id":9112,"date":"2024-08-29T07:00:00","date_gmt":"2024-08-29T07:00:00","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/landobuilderscorp.com\/?p=9112"},"modified":"2026-05-27T06:02:42","modified_gmt":"2026-05-27T06:02:42","slug":"life-while-your-home-is-being-remodeled","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/life-while-your-home-is-being-remodeled\/","title":{"rendered":"Life While Your Home Is Being Remodeled?"},"content":{"rendered":"\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">&#8220;<em>Life While Your Home Is Being Remodeled?<\/em>&#8220;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Living through a home remodel can be both exciting and challenging. Whether you&#8217;re renovating your kitchen, bathroom, basement, or the entire house, the decision to stay in your home during construction or temporarily relocate is not to be taken lightly. There are several factors to consider to ensure your comfort and safety amidst the chaos. Drawing from our extensive experience with clients, <a href=\"https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/\" title=\"\">Harris &amp; Sons<\/a> has compiled this comprehensive guide to help you navigate life during a home remodel. Our expert tips and insights will ensure a smoother, more manageable experience as you transform your living space.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img decoding=\"async\" src=\"https:\/\/landobuilderscorp.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/05\/home-improvement-renovation-and-remodeling-with-a-2023-11-27-05-25-26-utc-1024x729.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-9116\"\/><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Should You Stay or Should You Go?<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The decision to stay in your home during a remodel or move out temporarily depends on several factors, including the extent of the renovation, your tolerance for disruption, and your family\u2019s needs. Here are some considerations:<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">&#8211; Extent of Renovation: <\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">If you are remodeling a single room or a few rooms, you might be able to stay and use the rest of your home. However, if you are undertaking a whole-house renovation, temporary housing during the remodel might be more practical.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">&#8211; Cost Considerations: <\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Staying in your home will save you the cost of renting a hotel or apartment. However, living on-site may extend the project&#8217;s duration as contractors will need to work around your living spaces.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">&#8211; Convenience: <\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Living at home allows you to be on-site, facilitating better communication with contractors and enabling you to make quick decisions as needed.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">&#8211; Comfort and Safety: <\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Depending on the scale of the renovation, the noise, dust, and disruption can be significant. Consider the well-being of your family, including kids and pets, when deciding.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img decoding=\"async\" src=\"https:\/\/landobuilderscorp.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/05\/sharing-his-remodeling-progress-on-social-media-2023-11-27-05-19-44-utc-1024x683.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-9117\"\/><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Tips for Living at Home During Renovation<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">If you choose to stay in your home during the remodel, here are some tips to help you manage:<\/p>\n\n\n\n<ol class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Create a Temporary Living Space<\/strong>: Set up a temporary kitchen and living area. For example, if your kitchen is under renovation, create a small cooking space in another room with essential appliances like a microwave, toaster oven, and mini-fridge.<br><\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Protect Your Belongings<\/strong>: Cover furniture and valuables with plastic sheets or moving blankets to protect them from dust and damage. Label and store items securely.<br><\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Plan for Bathroom Access<\/strong>: If your bathroom is being remodeled, make arrangements for an alternate bathroom. Portable toilets can be rented if necessary.<br><\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Manage Dust and Debris<\/strong>: Discuss dust control measures with your contractor. Use plastic sheeting to seal off construction areas and consider investing in an air purifier to keep the air clean.<br><\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Maintain Daily Routines<\/strong>: Try to keep a sense of normalcy by sticking to your usual routines as much as possible. This can help reduce stress and make the experience more manageable.<br><\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Safety First<\/strong>: Ensure that construction zones are off-limits to kids and pets. Install temporary barriers if needed to keep everyone safe.<br><\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Communication with Contractors<\/strong>: Establish clear communication with your contractors. Regular updates on the progress and timeline will help you plan and adapt as needed.<br><\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Handling Noise and Disruption<\/strong>: Noise can be a significant issue. Use noise-canceling headphones or earplugs, and schedule noisy work for times when you&#8217;re less likely to be home.<br><\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Plan for Utility Disruptions<\/strong>: Be prepared for temporary disruptions to utilities like water, gas, and electricity. Have backup plans in place, such as bottled water and alternate cooking methods.<br><\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Budgeting for Unexpected Expenses<\/strong>: Keep a contingency fund for unexpected expenses. Renovations often uncover hidden issues that need to be addressed.<br><\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Protecting Pets<\/strong>: Consider boarding your pets or setting up a safe and quiet area for them away from the construction zone.<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Temporary Housing Options<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">If the renovation is extensive, moving out might be the best option. Here are some alternatives:<\/p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Stay with Family or Friends<\/strong>: This can be a cost-effective option, but be mindful of the potential for disrupting their lives.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Rent a Hotel Room<\/strong>: Many families choose to stay at a hotel for a few days or weeks. Look for long-term stay options with kitchen facilities to make your stay more comfortable.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Rent an Apartment<\/strong>: If the renovation will take several months, renting an apartment might be more practical.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Staying Organized During the Renovation<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Staying organized is key to managing a home remodel:<\/p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Create a Renovation Schedule<\/strong>: Work with your contractor to establish a clear timeline for the project. Knowing the schedule will help you plan and reduce stress.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Set Boundaries with Workers<\/strong>: Establish working hours and discuss areas of the home that are off-limits.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Involve Your Family<\/strong>: Involve your family in the planning process. This can help everyone feel more in control and less stressed.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Planning Outdoor Space Use<\/strong>: If your indoor space is limited, make use of outdoor areas for living and dining.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img decoding=\"async\" src=\"https:\/\/landobuilderscorp.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/05\/process-for-under-construction-remodeling-renova-2023-11-27-05-11-40-utc-1024x683.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-9118\"\/><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Post-Renovation Cleanup and Organization<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Once the renovation is complete, you\u2019ll need to clean and organize your home:<\/p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Deep Cleaning<\/strong>: Thoroughly clean your home to remove dust and debris. This includes carpets, upholstery, and all surfaces.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Organize Your Space<\/strong>: Take the opportunity to declutter and organize your space as you move back in.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Enjoy Your New Space<\/strong>: Finally, take the time to enjoy your newly remodeled home. Celebrate the completion of the project with your family and friends.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Conclusion<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Living through a home remodel in places like Bend, OR, Redmond, or Tigard, OR, can be challenging, but with careful planning and organization, it is possible to minimize the disruption. Whether you choose to stay in your home or temporarily relocate, understanding what to expect and preparing accordingly can make the experience more manageable. Remember to maintain open communication with your contractors, protect your belongings, and prioritize safety to ensure a smooth renovation process.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">At <a href=\"https:\/\/share.google\/gwM2ovux57i85a4fn\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Harris &amp; Sons<\/a>, we have extensive experience working with clients to ensure that your renovation are executed at the highest level. With the insights and tips provided, your remodeling project can become a seamless and enjoyable experience. Explore our Remodeling Services: <a title=\"\" href=\"https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/kitchen-remodeling\/\">Kitchens<\/a>, <a href=\"https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/bathroom-remodeling\/\">Bathrooms<\/a>, <a href=\"https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/basement-remodeling\/\">Basements<\/a> &amp; More, and let us help transform your home into the space you&#8217;ve always dreamed of. We look forward to <a href=\"https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/contact-us\/\" data-type=\"link\" data-id=\"https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/contact-us\/\">your call<\/a> and are eager to start planning your renovation journey with you.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><\/p>\n","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>&#8220;Life While Your Home Is Being Remodeled?&#8220; Living through a home remodel can be both exciting and challenging. Whether you&#8217;re renovating your kitchen, bathroom, basement, or the entire house, the decision to stay in your home during construction or temporarily relocate is not to be taken lightly. There are several factors to consider to ensure [&hellip;]<\/p>\n","protected":false},"author":1,"featured_media":9115,"comment_status":"open","ping_status":"open","sticky":false,"template":"","format":"standard","meta":{"_acf_changed":false,"footnotes":""},"categories":[33,30,32],"tags":[],"class_list":["post-9112","post","type-post","status-publish","format-standard","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","category-remodeling-tips","category-bathroom-resources","category-kitchen-resources"],"acf":[],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts\/9112","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts"}],"about":[{"href":"https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/post"}],"author":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/users\/1"}],"replies":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/comments?post=9112"}],"version-history":[{"count":5,"href":"https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts\/9112\/revisions"}],"predecessor-version":[{"id":16274,"href":"https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts\/9112\/revisions\/16274"}],"wp:attachment":[{"href":"https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media?parent=9112"}],"wp:term":[{"taxonomy":"category","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/categories?post=9112"},{"taxonomy":"post_tag","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/tags?post=9112"}],"curies":[{"name":"wp","href":"https:\/\/api.w.org\/{rel}","templated":true}]}}